# Build-context hygiene (context = repo root, shared by both images).
# Keeps node_modules / build artifacts / VCS / heavy data out of image builds.

**/node_modules
**/target
.git
.playwright-mcp
.claude/worktrees
web/build
web/.svelte-kit

# Secrets
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Databases — EXCLUDE ALL except the one the web BUILD reads at SSG time:
#   db/quran/tanzil/arabic/quran-uthmani.sqlite (node:sqlite: verse text)
# Surah metadata is committed JSON (web/static/quran-meta/); quran-data.xml
# is backend-only (Dockerfile.api). The api image creates its own easyquran.db at
# runtime; translation/simple-clean sqlite are never needed to build.
*.db
*.db-*
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite-shm
**/*.sqlite-wal
db/quran/tanzil/translations/sqlite
db/quran/tanzil/arabic/quran-simple-clean.sqlite
!db/quran/tanzil/arabic/quran-uthmani.sqlite

EasyQuran Website.dc.html
